# Criterion 3 - three states, distinguishable without grepping

## The legend, verbatim from docs/architecture/contracts-map.md

| Status | Means |
| --- | --- |
| **Live** | Production code in `lib/` is typed on the contract and runs against it. Swapping the implementation changes behavior. |
| **No production consumer** | An implementation exists, and for some rows a provider binds it to the contract, but nothing in `lib/` reads that binding. Tests may. Swapping the implementation changes nothing until a consumer exists. |
| **No implementor** | The contract is declared and nothing anywhere implements it. |

## The Status cell of every swap-map row (other cells elided)

  `INetworkClient`                                 **Live**
  `ApiClient` (concrete class, not a contract)     **Live**
  `IHttpResponseCache`                             **Live**
  `IKeyValueStore`                                 **Live**
  `ITokenStore`                                    **Live**
  `ISessionTerminationSink`                        **Live**
  `AppNavigator`                                   **No production consumer**
  `AppDesignTokens`                                **No production consumer**
  `IAuthController`                                **No production consumer**
  `ITasksController`                               **No implementor**

## Counts, over the swap-map rows only (the legend table is excluded)

  **Live**                       6 row(s)
  **No production consumer**     3 row(s)
  **No implementor**             1 row(s)

  total swap-map rows            10

# Three distinct status values are in use, and every row carries exactly one.
